WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:03.060
Gold Fever!

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:12.650
Wild Dun-

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:22.330
Storm Wolf makes the first point!

00:00:22.330 --> 00:00:25.330
Their swift offense surges right at the beginning of the match!

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.100
That... can't be...

00:00:37.490 --> 00:00:38.230
Damn it!

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:41.220
I can't believe he got through...

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:43.510
And did you see that speed?

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:48.720
Since the time he began his attack and made the shoot, it only took him 3.2 seconds.

00:00:49.110 --> 00:00:52.490
I knew they were fast, but not <i>this</i>  fast...

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:56.450
This is the power of Storm Wolf...

00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.360
That doesn't change anything!

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.910
We've trained ourselves in the Black Room!

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:05.150
Leave this to us, Ibuki!

00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:07.640
We'll score that point back before you even know it!

00:01:09.360 --> 00:01:11.210
That can't be...

00:01:12.110 --> 00:01:14.500
How could I have not been able to stop that?

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:17.370
I'll stop it this time!

00:01:20.620 --> 00:01:23.770
As long as we keep him back, their goalkeeper's got more holes than a colander.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:27.240
This match is gonna be so easy.

00:01:27.240 --> 00:01:30.190
Don't let your guard down, or you'll lose focus.

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.190
I got it.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:18.480
Football Frontier International V2's Asia district preliminaries finals!

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:26.100
The match between Japan's Inazuma Japan and Uzbekistan's Storm Wolf opens with Storm Wolf's whirlwind shoot!

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:29.570
It's still one point!

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:30.890
We'll take it back!

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:32.190
Yeah!

00:03:33.680 --> 00:03:35.830
Do your best, you'll need it.

00:03:40.640 --> 00:03:43.660
The match resumes with the kickoff by Inazuma Japan!

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:47.120
We can't afford to lose any more points!

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:48.570
Matatagi!

00:03:48.570 --> 00:03:49.040
Okay!

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:50.620
Sakura!

00:03:51.570 --> 00:03:53.790
Inazuma Japan moves up with their passes!

00:03:54.310 --> 00:03:56.020
It's no use.

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:56.540
Loran!

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.390
Storm Wolf goes in to stop them!

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.050
Sakura!

00:04:02.300 --> 00:04:04.340
Nozaki gets through!

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:05.930
All right!

00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:08.440
Yes!

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:10.470
That's it, Sakura-san! Keep it up!

00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:13.480
I'm not letting them steal the ball from me that easily!

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:15.810
I've trained so hard.

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:21.850
Losing to Resistance Japan has made us stronger.

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:25.240
Now, no matter who we're up against, we won't lose!

00:04:25.570 --> 00:04:26.990
Nozaki moves up!

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:28.490
We'll stop you!

00:04:30.220 --> 00:04:32.650
Rolling Cutter!

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.920
Storm Wolf's defense stops Nozaki in her tracks!

00:04:41.330 --> 00:04:43.780
I told you it wasn't any use.

00:04:44.080 --> 00:04:45.010
Mica! {ミーチャ}

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:48.260
Move up, Loran!

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:49.100
Our second point!

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:52.260
It's Storm Wolf's turn to counterattack!

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:53.600
I'll stop you!

00:04:57.980 --> 00:05:00.480
Defense Equation!

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.320
Good job, Manabe!

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.780
Manabe makes a good defense!

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.290
It's turning into a fierce game!

00:05:13.290 --> 00:05:14.830
Neither side is giving in!

00:05:15.150 --> 00:05:17.590
Go, Hayato-niichan!

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.710
You can do it, Inazuma Japan!

00:05:20.370 --> 00:05:21.370
They aren't losing.

00:05:21.370 --> 00:05:22.990
They're all doing their best!

00:05:22.990 --> 00:05:24.630
The results of their training.

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:28.180
From that dribbling, they'll come through me...

00:05:28.390 --> 00:05:29.390
From the left!

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.390
Now Inazuma Japan has the ball back!

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:38.250
Those moves... They're clearly different from the matches they've played before.

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.180
When did they obtain power like this?

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:44.610
They've got more power than I thought.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:48.200
Not that it's any comparison to ours.

00:05:53.330 --> 00:05:54.640
What is this feeling?

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:56.160
Something is wrong...

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.130
Who will make the next point?

00:05:59.130 --> 00:06:03.680
Will Inazuma Japan tie the score or will Storm Wolf pull ahead?!

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:08.180
The next point will have a great impact on the flow of the game!

00:06:08.930 --> 00:06:11.390
Matatagi moves up!

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:13.890
He's getting cocky.

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.670
Mica, Sergei!

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.100
Matatagi, over here!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:24.860
Rolling Cutter!

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:28.150
Matatagi!

00:06:28.150 --> 00:06:28.990
Nii-chan!

00:06:29.310 --> 00:06:30.280
To Dmitri!

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:31.530
I know!

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:33.030
Dmitri!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.370
Storm Wolf passes the ball in one move!

00:06:37.540 --> 00:06:37.910
Oh no!

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:42.290
Show no mercy!

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:43.040
Maxim!

00:06:44.990 --> 00:06:46.090
I'll stop them!

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:48.920
Gold Fever!

00:06:56.860 --> 00:06:58.600
Wild Dun-

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:00.850
It's in!

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.930
The next goal is made by Storm Wolf!

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:07.860
The point difference has widened to 2-0!

00:07:12.880 --> 00:07:15.120
Just look at that face.

00:07:15.350 --> 00:07:18.290
Shouldn't they have expected it? Our difference in power is just too big.

00:07:19.240 --> 00:07:20.040
Why...

00:07:20.860 --> 00:07:22.850
Why can't I stop them?!

00:07:27.950 --> 00:07:31.850
Coach Kuroiwa, are you sure this is going to be okay?

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:34.260
Ibuki-kun...

00:07:36.660 --> 00:07:39.040
It's still the early stages of the game!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:41.450
We'll take back a point first!

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:45.060
Both teams are in position.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:48.020
The score is 2-0 with Storm Wolf in the lead.

00:07:48.020 --> 00:07:51.280
If Inazuma Japan loses any more points, it's going to cost them.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:54.880
Nii-chan, Hayato-niichan won't lose, right?

00:07:54.880 --> 00:07:58.410
Of course not. He'd never lose.

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.460
Let's get this over this.

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:06.710
I'm sorry to be saying this about Ibuki, but I can't leave the goal to him any longer.

00:08:07.260 --> 00:08:10.760
<i>I'll</i>  stop Storm Wolf's attacks.

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:16.270
It seems that our intelligence alone is needed to break this deadlock.

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:17.550
Let's do it.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:19.790
The two of us will protect the goal together.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:24.750
If they score another point, there's only one answer for us no matter what equation I use:

00:08:24.750 --> 00:08:25.900
We lose.

00:08:26.370 --> 00:08:28.900
We'll get one point first... and that will be from me!

00:08:29.620 --> 00:08:31.690
I'll change the flow of the game!

00:08:34.310 --> 00:08:37.160
The match resumes with Inazuma Japan's kickoff!

00:08:39.510 --> 00:08:40.580
Matatagi!

00:08:42.190 --> 00:08:42.870
It's mine!

00:08:44.570 --> 00:08:47.170
Inazuma Japan suddenly has the ball stolen from them!

00:08:48.330 --> 00:08:51.440
I can't believe they made it all the way to the finals like that.

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:52.380
Move up, Loran!

00:08:52.880 --> 00:08:53.640
Loran!

00:08:53.640 --> 00:08:54.550
Okay!

00:08:55.420 --> 00:08:57.140
I'll stop him!

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:58.420
Maxim!

00:08:58.420 --> 00:08:59.140
Yeah!

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:03.180
Minaho-kun, work with me!

00:09:04.040 --> 00:09:11.320
If I come in from the right at 30 degrees, they'll focus on my position in response to any approach from the front and make a parabolic dodge!

00:09:12.150 --> 00:09:15.200
By predicting that move, we can stop him!

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:19.950
No, judging from his movements, I should go from the left.

00:09:19.950 --> 00:09:21.450
Back me up!

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.910
The defense is falling apart!

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.790
Then I won't hold back!

00:09:29.110 --> 00:09:29.920
What?!

00:09:31.570 --> 00:09:35.210
Inazuma Japan meets with them boldly but they can't take back the ball!

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:39.000
What's wrong?

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.600
They're all acting strangely!

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:42.140
Coach Kuroiwa!

00:09:46.330 --> 00:09:49.100
Nozaki is covering the front of the goal!

00:09:50.190 --> 00:09:52.630
Silk Road!

00:09:55.170 --> 00:09:56.900
This is a shoot chance for Loran!

00:09:57.710 --> 00:09:59.240
What am I doing wrong?

00:09:59.770 --> 00:10:03.040
I was able to stop balls at level 4 easily!

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.790
Kusaka manages to block it!

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:09.570
I see.

00:10:09.570 --> 00:10:12.460
Everyone's trying to cover for Ibuki on top of their own responsibilities...

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:13.920
Ironic.

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:18.370
Their rash way of gaining more power is having the opposite effect.

00:10:18.370 --> 00:10:19.640
What do we do, Tenma?

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:22.680
At this rate, not only will we fall behind, we won't even be able to steal the ball.

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:30.570
I'm always right here.

00:10:30.570 --> 00:10:32.080
Use me.

00:10:32.080 --> 00:10:34.910
I'll move exactly where you order me to go.

00:10:34.910 --> 00:10:38.310
It's just up to you to realize that first.

00:10:38.310 --> 00:10:43.070
If you can't realize that for yourself, you won't be able to make your best plays.

00:10:44.750 --> 00:10:45.870
Kusaka moves up!

00:10:46.390 --> 00:10:47.800
I'll stop you!

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:48.870
Kusaka, over here!

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:52.220
I'm gonna score this one first!

00:10:52.220 --> 00:10:52.880
Kusaka!

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:55.300
Rolling Cutter!

00:11:01.510 --> 00:11:03.720
But Matsukaze clears it!

00:11:04.730 --> 00:11:06.390
That play...

00:11:06.390 --> 00:11:07.970
It was just like me then...

00:11:13.260 --> 00:11:14.230
Ibuki, over here!

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.280
I'm gonna score this one first!

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:22.660
<i>Ibuki.</i>

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:27.120
<i>Is getting the ball with your own hands what you consider a good play?</i>

00:11:27.930 --> 00:11:29.200
I see...

00:11:32.080 --> 00:11:34.050
So that was it...

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.050
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:44.930
Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy!

00:11:46.730 --> 00:11:49.890
I started up basketball when I first entered junior high school.

00:11:50.880 --> 00:11:55.290
I could tell right away that I had a talent for basketball.

00:11:56.680 --> 00:12:02.650
I could cut the other team's passes easily, and I had no trouble making shoots.

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:05.950
Come on!

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.080
Let's see if you can take the ball from me!

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:13.490
Because of me, the team kept winning.

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:16.180
We won in all sorts of tournaments.

00:12:16.530 --> 00:12:17.040
But...

00:12:18.460 --> 00:12:20.520
One day, it all went wrong.

00:12:22.170 --> 00:12:23.720
Pass the ball?

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:29.020
You aren't playing the game by yourself! Quit hogging all the action!

00:12:29.020 --> 00:12:32.420
Sorry, but I don't take orders from anyone.

00:12:32.420 --> 00:12:34.530
I make my own rules.

00:12:34.530 --> 00:12:35.230
Ibuki!

00:12:35.770 --> 00:12:39.530
Who do you think is responsible for helping you guys win, anyway?

00:12:39.530 --> 00:12:42.970
It's your job as average nobodies to be following after me.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:47.450
At least try your hardest to keep up with my pace.

00:12:49.750 --> 00:12:52.370
After that, the team stopped winning.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:55.250
I couldn't agree with it.

00:12:56.640 --> 00:13:00.490
If I teamed up with failures like them, <i>my</i>  talent would be wasted!

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:06.380
That's why I agreed to Kuroiwa's offer.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:11.340
With the condition that I get to study abroad on a famous basketball team overseas.

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:17.150
But I was wrong.

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:20.440
We didn't win because they sucked at playing.

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:23.690
It was my fault for thinking that me being there was enough for us to win.

00:13:29.040 --> 00:13:31.830
The match resumes with the throw-in by Storm Wolf!

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:34.290
Will Storm Wolf's passes connect?

00:13:36.080 --> 00:13:37.960
But Nozaki cuts for it!

00:13:38.570 --> 00:13:40.210
And she continues with dribbling!

00:13:41.020 --> 00:13:41.960
Pass to Matatagi!

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:43.880
I'll get it this time!

00:13:43.880 --> 00:13:44.460
Sakura!

00:13:45.370 --> 00:13:47.760
Rolling Cutter!

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:52.060
Inazuma Japan's offense isn't coming together!

00:13:54.910 --> 00:13:55.390
Ruslan!

00:13:56.860 --> 00:13:58.060
It's time we made in another!

00:13:59.350 --> 00:14:00.580
Leave this to me!

00:14:01.130 --> 00:14:03.360
I'll stop him!

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:07.780
He dodges Tetsukado!

00:14:08.840 --> 00:14:09.990
Make it in, Maxim!

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.950
Gold Fever!

00:14:18.080 --> 00:14:20.170
Will this be the deciding third goal?!

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:25.460
Wild Dunk!

00:14:28.950 --> 00:14:29.930
Is it in?!

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:34.140
I-Ibuki stops it!

00:14:34.570 --> 00:14:35.310
Yes!

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:36.220
Too slow!

00:14:37.330 --> 00:14:37.950
No!

00:14:37.950 --> 00:14:39.310
He can't block it from there!

00:14:39.310 --> 00:14:40.560
You're finished!

00:14:53.220 --> 00:14:54.870
SHINDOU, HELP ME!

00:15:04.210 --> 00:15:06.030
Einsatz!

00:15:10.680 --> 00:15:15.410
Inazuma Japan's Ibuki and Shindou barely manage to block the third goal!

00:15:16.660 --> 00:15:18.460
You got lucky.

00:15:18.460 --> 00:15:19.890
They did it, they did it!

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:22.400
They stopped it! Right? Right?

00:15:22.400 --> 00:15:23.420
Yes!

00:15:23.420 --> 00:15:26.360
Getting all excited because they stopped one shoot... They're so easy to please.

00:15:27.620 --> 00:15:29.690
Looks like you finally get it.

00:15:30.910 --> 00:15:34.840
Defending the goal on your own isn't what you should be doing.

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:37.160
It's defending the goal after everyone else has pitched in.

00:15:37.750 --> 00:15:39.870
Take a good look at what's happening here on this field.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:49.410
I leave the rest to you.

00:15:50.590 --> 00:15:52.340
You'll be fine now.

00:15:53.110 --> 00:15:57.100
Tenma, I'm moving up too and joining the offense.

00:15:58.170 --> 00:15:59.010
Okay!

00:16:01.750 --> 00:16:02.770
Yes!

00:16:03.280 --> 00:16:06.050
That Ibuki asked Shindou for help...

00:16:06.270 --> 00:16:11.990
What's important isn't who defends the goal, but how to defend it together, huh?

00:16:12.930 --> 00:16:17.700
But I tried to defend it all on my own because I didn't think I could depend on Ibuki...

00:16:17.880 --> 00:16:22.080
It looks like we had a huge misunderstanding.

00:16:22.080 --> 00:16:22.710
Yeah.

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:24.770
Minaho-kun.

00:16:24.770 --> 00:16:25.710
Yeah.

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:29.410
Play while trusting other people?

00:16:29.860 --> 00:16:35.090
They have no idea how big of a disappointment it feels when those same people betray you.

00:16:36.400 --> 00:16:38.840
Now, it's Storm Wolf's throw-in!

00:16:38.840 --> 00:16:42.930
Will Inazuma Japan's momentum lead them to a goal this time?!

00:16:46.840 --> 00:16:48.580
You won't have it!

00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:51.230
Kusaka!

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:54.170
Inazuma Japan's pass goes through!

00:16:54.170 --> 00:16:56.320
Kusaka moves up dribbling!

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.230
We'll stop you!

00:16:59.790 --> 00:17:00.410
Kusaka!

00:17:00.990 --> 00:17:01.700
Captain!

00:17:02.800 --> 00:17:03.410
Kusaka!

00:17:10.110 --> 00:17:12.590
Inazuma Japan's passes connect!

00:17:12.590 --> 00:17:13.420
Guys!

00:17:13.660 --> 00:17:14.840
They finally realize it.

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.370
I'll go from the left!

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:18.590
What about you, Manabe-kun?

00:17:18.590 --> 00:17:21.930
I'll run a parallel tangent from contrast point B!

00:17:22.530 --> 00:17:24.890
Minaho and Manabe stop him!

00:17:26.560 --> 00:17:29.940
Leaf Roll!

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:34.700
This time, Morimura uses a hissatsu technique!

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.420
This can work!

00:17:36.420 --> 00:17:38.410
The team is fighting as one!

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:40.820
W-What happened to them?

00:17:40.820 --> 00:17:42.590
Nothing happened.

00:17:42.590 --> 00:17:45.960
Their gears have just started locking together.

00:17:46.790 --> 00:17:50.670
So we finally get to play against a decent opponent, huh?

00:17:54.590 --> 00:17:58.840
Neither Storm Wolf nor Inazuma Japan is giving in!

00:17:58.840 --> 00:18:00.820
The clock is ticking on the first half!

00:18:00.820 --> 00:18:03.600
Will we reach halftime with a score of 2-0 still?

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:06.390
You can do it, everyone!

00:18:07.510 --> 00:18:10.560
Oh no, Storm Wolf gets through!

00:18:11.280 --> 00:18:11.930
Ibuki!

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:13.070
Score, Maxim!

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:17.280
Manabe! Minaho!

00:18:17.640 --> 00:18:18.190
Yeah!

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:19.240
Leave it to us!

00:18:21.840 --> 00:18:23.660
Now his course is limited.

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.250
His only choice is to come in through the center.

00:18:28.240 --> 00:18:28.830
Here he comes!

00:18:29.110 --> 00:18:31.630
Gold Fever!

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:43.630
Rising Slash!

00:18:48.950 --> 00:18:49.860
What?!

00:18:49.860 --> 00:18:51.230
It's a new hissatsu technique!

00:18:51.270 --> 00:18:55.980
Ibuki stops Maxim's hissatsu shoot with his new hissatsu technique!

00:19:00.390 --> 00:19:02.730
We did it, Minaho, Manabe!

00:19:02.730 --> 00:19:03.240
Yes!

00:19:03.240 --> 00:19:04.370
Yeah!

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:10.370
Ibuki, I'll make sure this ball you've stopped leads to a goal.

00:19:10.750 --> 00:19:11.920
Tenma! Nozaki!

00:19:12.370 --> 00:19:12.880
Okay!

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:15.130
Let's go, Nozaki!

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:16.800
Captain!

00:19:17.440 --> 00:19:19.820
Inazuma Japan goes for its counterattack!

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:20.510
Yuri!

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:21.890
I'll stop you!

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.250
Z Slash!

00:19:27.570 --> 00:19:29.560
Matsukaze gets past!

00:19:30.350 --> 00:19:31.450
Tsurugi!

00:19:32.710 --> 00:19:34.690
Bicycle Sword!

00:19:37.730 --> 00:19:38.840
It's in!

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:41.700
Inazuma Japan finally takes back a point!

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:43.160
What?!

00:19:56.770 --> 00:19:58.800
There's the whistle ending the first half!

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:03.800
The score is 2-1! Storm Wolf has a small one point lead!

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:07.560
Now there's no telling where the match will go from here!

00:20:08.020 --> 00:20:11.070
You did great, everyone! You took back a point first!

00:20:11.280 --> 00:20:12.810
Tsurugi-kun, nice shoot!

00:20:15.440 --> 00:20:17.980
Good job too, Ibuki-kun, with your new hissatsu technique!

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:24.460
Ibuki, when did you come up with a hissatsu like that?

00:20:24.460 --> 00:20:26.120
Because of your training, right?

00:20:26.660 --> 00:20:29.290
No, it was thanks to Manabe and Minaho.

00:20:32.680 --> 00:20:37.910
I was able to concentrate on the ball because Manabe and Minaho blocked his course.

00:20:37.910 --> 00:20:41.920
As long as I can concentrate, stopping a shoot like that is a piece of cake.

00:20:43.130 --> 00:20:45.330
Is he being grateful to us?

00:20:45.330 --> 00:20:48.010
Or is he just bragging?

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:51.940
What.

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.040
All right, everyone!

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.150
We'll catch up to them in the second half!

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:01.320
Yeah!

00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:09.260
They're so hyper over one point.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:11.350
So carefree.

00:21:11.350 --> 00:21:15.670
But that one point can cause the game to change dramatically.

00:21:16.510 --> 00:21:20.210
We'll widen the gap between us in the second half before that happens!

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:23.980
Inazuma Japan.

00:21:24.460 --> 00:21:26.360
We will be the winners!

00:22:53.930 --> 00:22:56.680
This is the way to make the impossible possible!

00:22:56.680 --> 00:23:00.970
And when it all comes to an end, a new shock arrives!

00:23:00.970 --> 00:23:03.680
Next, The End And the Beginning Of The Battle.

00:23:03.680 --> 00:23:05.860
This is super-dimensional soccer!

00:23:15.130 --> 00:23:19.580
The Inazuma Eleven GO Galaxy's proverb today is...

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:26.570
If you can't realize that for yourself, you won't be able to make your best plays!

00:23:26.570 --> 00:23:27.540
That's all!
